From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 05:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Link the GPU to its CLPC

The J604 enables the PMC (t8132-j604.dts &pmc, static voter agent 3 from
the J604 ADT), so its CLPC child from t8132-memory.dtsi probes. Point the
GPU at that CLPC with apple,clpc, so the G16 driver reports its work there
and the T8132 memory floor follows GPU work in flight instead of the GFX
power state, which the G16 firmware keeps on while the GPU idles.

This is the J604 copy of commit 26c2e08a9b89 ("arm64: dts: apple:
t8132-j713: Link the GPU to its CLPC"), which links only the J713 because
the other T8132 boards leave the PMC disabled.

Not yet measured on the J604 (needs an on-device run).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
index c1b60a4644..5ddd22964b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@
 		/* G16 is admitted on non-coherent DMA only. */
 		dma-noncoherent;
 		apple,pmp = <&pmp>;
+		apple,clpc = <&clpc>;
 		memory-region = <&gpu_ttbs>, <&gpu_pagetables>, <&gpu_handoff>,
 				<&gpu_shared_l2>, <&gpu_fw_text>, <&gpu_fw_data>;
 		memory-region-names = "ttbs", "pagetables", "handoff",
